The formula is:

[
\text{wind chill}=\text{air temperature}-0.7\cdot\text{wind speed}
]

In the sample, the fraction of fish that are trout is:

[
\frac{30}{180}=\frac{1}{6}
]

The line through $A(0,0)$ and $B(3,1)$ has equation:

[
y=\frac{x}{3}
]

The line through $C(0,10)$ and $D(2,9)$ has slope $-\frac12$, so:

[
y=10-\frac{x}{2}
]

Approximate $6.5$ months as:

[
6.5\cdot30=195\text{ days}
]

Convert days to hours:

[
195\cdot24=4680\text{ hours}
]

Divide by the large circle area:

[
\frac{\frac{11}{4}\pi}{9\pi}=\frac{11}{36}
]

His usual route is $10$ blocks and $\frac12$ mile, so one block is:

[
\frac{1/2}{10}=\frac1{20}\text{ mile}
]

The detour makes the next one-block segment become $3$ blocks, so he must walk:

[
3+4=7\text{ blocks}
]

That distance is:

[
7\cdot\frac1{20}=\frac7{20}=0.35\text{ mile}
]

Thus the completed table has:

[
133\text{ Ps},\ 134\text{ Qs},\ 133\text{ Rs}
]

Now compare one trapezoid to the inner triangle:

[
\frac{\frac5{27}A}{\frac49A}=\frac5{12}
]

The possible partitions into three disjoint triples are:

[
\{1,5,9\},\{2,6,7\},\{3,4,8\}
]

and

[
\{1,6,8\},\{2,4,9\},\{3,5,7\}
]

Each tile has probability $\frac14$ of being the needed orientation, so one fixed block has probability:

[
\left(\frac14\right)^4=\frac1{256}
]

So the events are disjoint, and the probability is:

[
4\cdot\frac1{256}=\frac1{64}
]
